%T A292428 1241464701561,65855927575486,3927668145225617,260989556256324950,
%U A292428 19173503690406046037,1546916066974914667700,136264803323322755652897
%N A292428 Number of matchings in the n-Andrásfai graph.
%H A292428 Vladeta Jovovic, <a href="/A292428/b292428.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..100</a>
%H A292428 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/AndrasfaiGraph.html">Andrásfai Graph</a>
%H A292428 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/IndependentEdgeSet.html">Independent Edge Set</a>
%H A292428 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Matching.html">Matching</a>
%F A292428 a(n) = [B*A*(C*B*A)^(n-1) 1]_{x=y=z=1}, where A = x + d/dz, B = y + d/dx, and C = z + d/dy. The operators act from right to left. - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Oct 26 2026
%e A292428 For n = 3, put P = (C*B*A)^2 1. Then
%e A292428 P = x^2*y^2*z^2 + 3*x^2*y*z + x*y^2*z + 3*x*y*z^2
%e A292428     + x^2 + 2*x*y + 5*x*z + 2*y*z + z^2 + 2.
%e A292428 B*A*P = x*y*P + y*P_z + P + x*P_x + P_xz.
%e A292428 At x = y = z = 1, we have P = 21, P_x = 21, P_z = 21 and P_xz = 22.
%e A292428 Hence a(3) = 2*21 + 21 + 21 + 22 = 106.
%K A292428 nonn,changed
